\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2.18}{\ignorespaces Pneumatic actuator grasping process of an egg \blx@tocontentsinit {0}\cite {yu2022modeling}: (a) The soft actuator moves toward the egg when pneumatic module one is pressurized to 10 kPa, with module two remaining at zero pressure. (b) Contact between the tip of the soft actuator and the egg occurs when the pressure in module one is increased to 20 kPa and module two is set to 14.1 kPa. (c) The egg is securely pinched by the gripper when both module one and module two are pressurized to 20 kPa. (d) The egg is held firmly when the supporting platform is removed, indicating a stable grasp by the gripper.}}{19}{figure.caption.42}%
